  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340646",
      "title": "Working with Parallel Routes & Nested Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 141,
      "videoOrder": 131,
      "sourceHash": "f948d566bb4c92adb2af00462931adb3b9f8902dc4893712a642400b2715d0ed",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 2.4,
          "en": "So, let's now build up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "on this parallel routing feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 6.78,
          "en": "and make it a bit more useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.78,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "Because of course, if all we wanted to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 14.52,
          "en": "is show two pieces of content on one at the same page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.52,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "we could have also solved that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "by simply including all that content into one single page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 24.9,
          "en": "We don't need two independent routes for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 29.37,
          "en": "But we will need that feature for what we're about to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.37,
          "end": 30.603,
          "en": "to this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 33.09,
          "en": "Because now I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.09,
          "end": 34.89,
          "en": "that here in this archive area,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 39.87,
          "en": "we can dive deeper into our news archive by, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "picking different years and by then only showing the news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 45.333,
          "en": "that belonged to a certain year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.56,
          "end": 49.53,
          "en": "To implement this, we can go to this archive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 54.53,
          "en": "page.js file here, and then by adding another route folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.08,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "next to it, because now, as I just explained,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 62.673,
          "en": "I wanna allow users to pick different years.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "So therefore, I wanna add a dynamic route segment here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 71.96000000000001,
          "en": "where we have the year that was picked as a placeholder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.97,
          "end": 75.85,
          "en": "and as a value that will be encoded in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.89,
          "end": 79.89,
          "en": "so that we can show those details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 84.89,
          "en": "or show a list of the use items that belong to this year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.73,
          "end": 90.18,
          "en": "In the page.js file one level above that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "so the page.js file in the archive folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 98.63,
          "en": "In that file, I now want to replace this h1 element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.97,
          "end": 103.97,
          "en": "with a header, which has an ID of \"archive-header\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 108.87,
          "en": "for styling purposes, where I wanna have a nav element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.87,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "which contains an unordered list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "which now outputs all the different years",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 115.25999999999999,
          "end": 117.39,
          "en": "of the different news items we have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 119.00999999999999,
          "en": "so that we can click those years",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.00999999999999,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "to go to the filtered list of news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 127.08,
          "en": "Now therefore, we need to find out which years exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 128.97,
          "en": "in our dummy-news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.97,
          "end": 131.19,
          "en": "And to simplify that process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.19,
          "end": 135.84,
          "en": "I prepared a little helper file, which you find attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.84,
          "end": 140.84,
          "en": "a news.js file, which I'll add into a brand new lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.07999999999998,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "which I'll add next to the components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 147.57,
          "en": "and it's up to you where you wanna add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.57,
          "end": 149.1,
          "en": "or how you want to name it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 149.1,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "But my idea is to have a folder that contains some helper,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 156.63,
          "en": "some utility code that's not components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.63,
          "end": 161.63,
          "en": "And in that lib folder, I stored that attached news.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.15,
          "end": 164.52,
          "en": "And in there, I simply got some functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 164.52,
          "end": 167.76,
          "en": "that operate on the dummy-news and that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 167.76,
          "end": 172.76,
          "en": "give me all the available years in a sorted order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 172.89,
          "end": 176.73,
          "en": "that can be identified from those dummy years.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.73,
          "end": 179.67000000000002,
          "en": "So simply some helper code that helps us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 179.67000000000002,
          "end": 181.443,
          "en": "deal with those news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 185.76,
          "en": "Back at the archive page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.76,
          "end": 190.76,
          "en": "we can now use that helper file to get the links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 191.22,
          "end": 196.22,
          "en": "that should be rendered by calling getAvailableNewsYears();",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 196.41,
          "end": 198.66,
          "en": "which is one of those utility functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "provided by that news file you find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 207.89,
          "en": "So that will simply give me an array of year identifiers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 207.9,
          "end": 212.01,
          "en": "so to say, and I'll use those to render my links here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 212.01,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "Therefore, in this unordered list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 217.77,
          "en": "I'll then use my links and convert these years",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 217.77,
          "end": 220.63,
          "en": "to actual links with the map function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 227.15,
          "en": "so that for every year I output a list item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 227.55,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "which has a key of link and which inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 236.57,
          "en": "then outputs a next link imported from next/link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 237.54,
          "end": 239.49,
          "en": "where the link path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 243.03,
          "en": "is actually a dynamically constructed path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 243.03,
          "end": 246.45,
          "en": "that starts with /archive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 246.45,
          "end": 250.29,
          "en": "but where we then have slash, and then the link value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 250.29,
          "end": 252.633,
          "en": "so the year identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 254.31,
          "end": 256.56,
          "en": "And it's also that year identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 256.56,
          "end": 260.343,
          "en": "that we can output here as text between the link text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 261.66,
          "end": 263.94,
          "en": "So, that will now output such a header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 263.94,
          "end": 268.2,
          "en": "inside of the page.js file in the @archive folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 268.2,
          "end": 270.63,
          "en": "And therefore now if you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 270.63,
          "end": 273.183,
          "en": "you should see these years here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 274.05,
          "end": 277.023,
          "en": "Now, if we click one of those years,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 278.07,
          "end": 280.563,
          "en": "we see that we actually get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 281.61,
          "end": 282.72,
          "en": "And I'm getting that error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 282.72,
          "end": 287.72,
          "en": "because the default export in my year page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 287.76,
          "end": 291.813,
          "en": "So, in that dynamic year folder is not a React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 292.65,
          "end": 294.33,
          "en": "And that is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 294.33,
          "end": 297.72,
          "en": "In that square bracket year folder, the page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 297.72,
          "end": 299.28,
          "en": "does not export anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 299.28,
          "end": 301.11,
          "en": "And of course, it should export something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 301.11,
          "end": 303.87,
          "en": "so that we have a page that can be displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 303.87,
          "end": 306.183,
          "en": "if a specific year was chosen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 310.14,
          "en": "So here, I'll have my FilteredNewsPage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 310.14,
          "end": 312.36,
          "en": "that sounds like a fitting name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 312.36,
          "end": 316.83,
          "en": "And in there, I essentially want to output a list of news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 316.83,
          "end": 320.97,
          "en": "just as I'm doing it in my main news page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 320.97,
          "end": 323.46,
          "en": "So, I want to have such an unordered list here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 323.46,
          "end": 326.82,
          "en": "and hence we can actually copy that, or better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 326.82,
          "end": 329.823,
          "en": "we can outsource it into a separate component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 330.69,
          "end": 335.69,
          "en": "So, in a components folder, I'll add a news-list.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 335.90999999999997,
          "end": 340.313,
          "en": "and export my NewsList component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 342.33,
          "end": 345.213,
          "en": "And I expect to get a prop named \"news\" here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 346.83,
          "end": 349.35,
          "en": "And then I'll return that unordered list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 349.35,
          "end": 353.43,
          "en": "with a class of news list where I will map through my news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 353.43,
          "end": 355.233,
          "en": "to output these news items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 359.55,
          "en": "And now in the main news page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 359.55,
          "end": 364.55,
          "en": "we can replace this unordered list here with my NewsList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 364.659,
          "end": 366.51,
          "en": "So, with this newly added component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 366.51,
          "end": 368.41,
          "en": "which therefore also must be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 369.63,
          "end": 372.6,
          "en": "And of course, there, we have to set the news prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 372.6,
          "end": 375.96,
          "en": "and set it to the dummy-news in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 375.96,
          "end": 377.73,
          "en": "And we can get rid of that link import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 377.73,
          "end": 379.65,
          "en": "since I'm not using that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 379.65,
          "end": 381.33299999999997,
          "en": "in this component anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 382.71,
          "end": 385.56,
          "en": "We can now also use this NewsList component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 385.56,
          "end": 389.223,
          "en": "here in this archive year page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 390.36,
          "end": 393.033,
          "en": "There, I want to output this NewsList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 393.987,
          "end": 398.7,
          "en": "And now the news must be set to the news that are filtered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 398.7,
          "end": 401.433,
          "en": "for that year that was chosen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 402.57,
          "end": 404.49,
          "en": "So, of course we can get access to that year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 404.49,
          "end": 406.71,
          "en": "by using the params prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 406.71,
          "end": 409.95,
          "en": "which we receive automatically by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 409.95,
          "end": 414.95,
          "en": "And then here, I got my newsYear by accessing params.year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 416.43,
          "end": 418.08,
          "en": "And of course, it's .year here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 418.08,
          "end": 420.75,
          "en": "because I chose year as an identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 420.75,
          "end": 422.313,
          "en": "between the square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 423.3,
          "end": 426.9,
          "en": "Now, I need to get all the news that belong to that year,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 426.9,
          "end": 431.37,
          "en": "and I added a utility function to that news.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 431.37,
          "end": 433.83,
          "en": "which we stored in that lib folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 433.83,
          "end": 438.83,
          "en": "because there you'll find the getNewsForYear function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 438.93,
          "end": 441,
          "en": "which simply filters the DUMMY_NEWS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 441,
          "end": 443.64300000000003,
          "en": "for news that belong to the chosen year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 444.9,
          "end": 447.94,
          "en": "And hence here, I got my news by calling getNewsForYear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 449.67,
          "end": 453.78,
          "en": "and by passing the newsYear to that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 453.78,
          "end": 456.9,
          "en": "And then, it's the news here that will be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 456.9,
          "end": 458.313,
          "en": "to the news list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 459.93,
          "end": 461.67,
          "en": "Now in the NewsList component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 461.67,
          "end": 464.1,
          "en": "we just also should make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
